{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And he instructed… saying.</b> The verse's saying <b>saying</b> is seemingly unnecessary — meaning, even if he does not ask in this formulation, but rather he should pose the question in language such that it will be understood from it that this is what he is asking." "<b>Or</b> it may mean that they are obligated to reply, even if the question will not be posed mouth to mouth to them, but rather he will ask a third party and the third party will ask them. And the verse's saying ״וּשְׁאֵלְךָ״ means either he himself, or that he will say to ask you. Or in this manner: ״וּשְׁאֵלְךָ״ — and the question will be [posed] through a third party, saying to you."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:36.305743526Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}